# lf104, the counted tale (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf104
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_tansy_sunmead
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the counted tale
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_things_under_the_breath
likes fried_fish old_tales market_bustle first_warm_day
dislikes flies rats
fears a_rat_in_the_linen_stores forgetting_the_ending_of_a_good_tale
hopes a_lively_market_after_a_long_winter a_tale_worth_repeating
topics pastimes +0.5 work +0.4 home +0.3 gossip +0.2
styles comfort=gentle gossip=playful refuse=plain tease=playful
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# counts #shuttle# passes under the breath, saves the best #tale# for the #market#, and checks the #linen# #store# for #rats#.

words
oath! = Shuttle and story | By the thirteenth thread
saying! = Leave one turn for the teller | Count the cloth, then count the cost
loom = loom | linen loom
shuttle = shuttle | wooden shuttle
shuttles = shuttles | spare shuttles
warp = warp | linen warp
weft = weft | crossing weft
thread = thread | linen thread
threads = threads | loose threads
linen = linen | woven linen
cloth = cloth | finished cloth
bolt = bolt | linen bolt
bolts = bolts | linen bolts
hem = hem | narrow hem
knot = knot | tight knot
knots = knots | tight knots
beam = beam | loom beam
shed = shed | weaving shed
store = store | linen store
shelf = shelf | storeroom shelf
shelves = shelves | high shelves
work = work | loom work
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | quick hands
count = count | whispered count
number = number | small number
numbers = numbers | whispered numbers
tale = tale | old tale
tales = tales | old tales
story = story | market story
ending = ending | proper ending
beginning = beginning | surprising beginning
listener = listener | patient listener
laugh = laugh | sudden laugh
joke = joke | sly joke
market = market | crowded market
stall = stall | market stall
seller = seller | loud seller
buyer = buyer | passing buyer
crowd = crowd | market crowd
road = road | High Road
gate = gate | town gate
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
city = city | Ridgemere
coin = coin | saved coin
price = price | marked price
wages = wages | weekly wages
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
table = table | supper table
plate = plate | supper plate
bread = bread | fresh bread
fish = fish | fried fish
butter = butter | melted butter
pan = pan | frying pan
cup = cup | small cup
jar = jar | friendly jar
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
visitor = visitor | new visitor
stranger = stranger | unfamiliar face
rat = rat | store rat
rats = rats | store rats
fly = fly | summer fly
flies = flies | summer flies
trap = trap | wooden trap
spring = spring | early spring
summer = summer | warm summer
winter = winter | long winter
warmth = warmth | first warmth
sun = sun | pale sun
rain = rain | light rain
wind = wind | field wind
field = field | open field
downs = downs | Larkdowns
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | late evening
day = day | long day
hour = hour | passing hour
door = door | cottage door
window = window | open window
bench = bench | plain bench
merchant = merchant | passing merchant
wagons = wagons | supply wagons
stories = stories | market stories
loaf = loaf | fresh loaf
endings = endings | proper endings
days = days | warm days
toll = toll | gate toll
coins = coins | saved coins
bird = bird | carved bird
feathers = feathers | carved feathers
wing = wing | wooden wing
music = music | festival music
floor = floor | wooden floor

any
opinion @1 church against 1 : A #plate# can make the rounds before a hungry #neighbour# gets #bread#. | I prefer to know where my #coin# lands.
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# has too many elbows for a good #tale#. | Nobody there waits for the #ending#.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : One #jar# shared after the #work# is pleasant company. | I know when my #cup# is full.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : Give me a dance, a #market# #crowd#, and someone who can finish a #story#. | I will rest in #winter#.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : They can reserve an empty #bench# while a working #hand# stands. | I notice who gets invited.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #price# of #bread# runs ahead of my #wages#. | A #merchant# calls it ordinary from behind full #shelves#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A newcomer should learn the #loom# before taking a #shuttle# from an older #hand#. | There is room after the #work# is shared.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The watch hears a #joke# from across the #market# and misses a missing #bolt#. | Let them count something useful.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I was at number twelve on this #bolt#. | #greet#. Have you heard the one about the #wagon#?
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Come in; I saved the #ending# for you. | There is #fish# beside your #plate#.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #loom# has had six passes already. | #greet#. The first #seller# is shouting at the #gate#.
line @1 greet.return : You are back before I finished counting. | I have thought of a better #ending#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Sit by the #table# while I finish this #thread#. | I kept the warm #bread# for you.
line @1 again.open : Did I tell you the first half? | The #market# was louder than yesterday.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have a #bolt# to count again. | Keep the #tale# until we meet.
line @1 farewell.return : Come when the #stall# closes. | I will save a new #joke#.
line @1 react.news : Begin at the surprising part. | Who heard it at the #market#?
line @1 react.news.new : No one in the #shed# has brought me that word. | Was the #wagon# late with it?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard an earlier version from a #seller#. | Your version has a better middle.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That #story# has a loose #thread#. | Which #listener# saw the thing happen?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I will stop joking. Tell me what you need. | The #work# can wait while you sit.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I would tell that twice at the #table#. | We should make room for another #plate#.
line @1 answer.how : The #bolt# is even and the #pan# held enough #fish#. | The #market# gave me two good #tales#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am keeping the #shuttle# moving. | The #warp# needs every #thread# counted.
line @1 ask.how : Did the #road# bring you a story? | Has the #market# been kind to you?
line @1 sympathise : I can leave the #joke# for another #day#. | Take the quiet place beside the #window#.
line @1 reassure : A missed #number# can be counted again. | The #spring# #sun# will come through this #winter#.
line @1 decline : No. I have not seen the #price# written down. | I must finish this #bolt# first.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair; leave the matter until after #supper#. | Then I will tell it another way.
line @1 thank : You found the missing #shuttle# under the #beam#. | That #bread# came just when I needed it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I was counting this way already. | It was only half a #plate#.
line @1 preclose : The #store# #door# needs checking for #rats#. | My #count# has slipped while we spoke.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You would lose a #shuttle# in an empty #shed#. | Your #tale# took longer than the #winter#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. That makes thirteen. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will ask the #seller#.
line @1 give.advice : Mark every tenth pass with a #knot# you can feel. | Keep the #fish# covered when the #flies# gather.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Wait for company before leaving by the #gate#. | I would stay near the #wagons#.
scene whispered_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count each #shuttle# pass under my breath. | If someone interrupts at twelve, I begin that #bolt# again.
b : Why not mark the number? | Does it take long?
a : My #hands# are busy. | Less than fixing a skipped #thread#.

scene knot_marker
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Every tenth pass gets a little #knot# at the edge. | I can find it by touch when the #shed# grows dim.
b : Does it show in the cloth? | Who taught you?
a : I trim it at the #hem#. | An older #hand# at this #loom#.

scene loose_weft
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A loose #weft# leaves a pale line across a whole #bolt#. | I stop the #shuttle# when my fingers feel one.
b : Can you mend it? | Does the buyer notice?
a : Before the #beam# takes it up. | If I leave it, certainly.

scene crowded_market
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like the #market# when every #stall# has a caller. | I can hear five #stories# before buying one #loaf#.
b : Do you remember them? | Is it noisy?
a : The good #endings#. | Loud enough to make me smile.

scene old_tale
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good old #tale# changes with the #listener#. | I keep the same #beginning# and let the middle breathe.
b : Is that cheating? | Do you know the ending?
a : Only if I pretend I did not. | I know several.

scene missing_ending
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once forgot the #ending# of a #tale# before the whole #table#. | I asked each #listener# to invent one.
b : Did they? | Which was best?
a : Until #evening#. | The shortest, to my surprise.

scene fried_fish
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fish in #butter# needs watching as closely as the #loom#. | Turn it once and let the edge crisp.
b : Do you fry it often? | Do the flies come?
a : When the #market# has some. | Only if I leave the #window# open.

scene fly_cover
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I cover the #plate# before a single #fly# finds it. | The #flies# are quicker on warm #days#.
b : Do they spoil supper? | What do you use?
a : If I let them. | A clean piece of #linen#.

scene rat_store
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #rat# can make a nest behind the #shelves# of the #store#. | I listen before moving a #bolt#.
b : Have you caught one? | Does it eat cloth?
a : With a #trap#, once. | It chews the ties.

scene first_warm_day
when topic=weather here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : On the first warm #spring# #day# I open the #shed# #door#. | The #warp# feels less stiff under my #hands#.
b : Do you stop to go outside? | Does it change the work?
a : At the next rest. | The #threads# move more freely.

scene wagon_story
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #wagon# driver paid the #gate# #toll# and told me a #tale# from the #city#. | I kept the funny part and doubted the rest.
b : What was funny? | Did you tell it again?
a : The driver was the punchline. | After checking a little.

scene market_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count my #coins# before I reach the #stall#. | A #seller# who changes the #price# mid-story loses my trade.
b : Has that happened? | Do you argue?
a : Once this #winter#. | I take my #coin# elsewhere.

scene shared_house
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# hears both paper hands and #loom# hands come #home#. | I wait until everyone is eating before a #tale#.
b : Is it crowded? | Do they listen?
a : At #supper#. | If I begin well.

scene friend_carving
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #friend# carved a little #bird# and left it by my #plate#. | I counted its #feathers# before saying thank you.
b : How many were there? | Do you still have it?
a : One fewer on the left #wing#. | On the #shelf#.

scene spring_dance
when topic=pastimes here.day=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I dance near the #market# #stall# until the #music# stops. | A full #day# outside beats a long #winter# inside.
b : Do you dance with anyone? | Are you tired after?
a : Whoever keeps the beat. | Happily so.

scene city_smoke
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #city# sends #wagons# with #cloth# and smoke clinging to the covers. | I would rather smell the #field# after #rain#.
b : Have you been there? | Is the cloth useful?
a : Once. | When the #thread# holds.

scene watch_count
when topic=news
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The watch counted raised voices at the #market# while a #bolt# went missing. | I kept my own #count# and found the gap.
b : Did they find the bolt? | Did they believe you?
a : Behind a #wagon#. | After they saw the #shelf#.

story thirteenth_pass [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : I reached thirteen #shuttle# passes and a #seller# called through the #shed# #door#.
  : I lost my place, so I counted the #threads# from the last #knot#.
  ask : Was the cloth sound?
  b : A better count than a guess.
  : The #bolt# came off even.

story borrowed_ending [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I began an old #tale# at the #table# and forgot how it ended.
  : A #friend# supplied a new #ending# so good I now ask for it each time.
  ask : Do you tell the original?
  b : Stories can grow.
  : Only when that #friend# is away.

story first_spring [topic=weather self.age>=18]
  : The first warm #spring# #day# came while I was tying a #hem#.
  : I opened the #window#, and the #market# noise carried into the #shed#.
  ask : Did you finish the work?
  b : Warm air helps.
  : Before the #sun# left the #field#.

rule @bark_count
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Twelve, thirteen, back to twelve. | That #knot# marks ten.

rule @bark_tale
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say I know a better #ending#. | The #beginning# is the easy part.

rule @bark_market
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #market# is calling already. | That #seller# has a loud voice.

rule @bark_store
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say I heard a #rat# behind the #shelf#. | Keep the #bolts# off the #floor#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have counted this #bolt# twice. | #greet#. Stay for the end of a #tale#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You are back before I found a new #ending#. | I remember you; how did that #story# turn out?
dlg @1 resident.job : My #shuttle# crosses #linen# at the #shed#. | I count the #weft# passes and tie off each #hem#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. My #count# is waiting. | #saying.capitalize#. Bring a #tale# next time.
graft resident.hub
choice Why count under your breath? -> count
node count
say Each #shuttle# pass matters. I whisper the #number# and mark every tenth with a little #knot#.
free
choice Tell me an old tale. -> tale
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node tale
say A #wagon# driver forgot a #story# ending at the #gate#. The #market# invented a better one.
choice Back to the loom. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I am at the next #knot#. | #greet#. I have a #tale# for you.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #bolt# needs one more #count#. | I will see you when the #market# quiets.
